ord_type": "comment", "crawl_source": "body_text", "keyword_match": false, "keyword_matches": [], "created_at_label": "5w", "parent_comment_id": ""}, {"url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DWRxQ-Djb8N/#comment-5", "text": "Cả nhà kéo xuống dưới cùng của phần caption, rồi ấn chữ “Dịch/Translate” để đọc công thức bằng tiếng Việt nha 😘", "author": "halseyskitchenn", "post_id": "DWRxQ-Djb8N", "created_at": "2026-03-27T08:05:35.228873+00:00", "external_id": "comment:halseyskitchenn|7w|c-nh-k-o-xu-ng-d-i-c-ng-c-a-ph-n-caption-r-i-n-ch-d-ch-translate-c", "record_type": "comment", "crawl_source": "body_text", "keyword_match": false, "keyword_matches": [], "created_at_label": "7w", "parent_comment_id": ""}], "platform": "instagram", "post_url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DWRxQ-Djb8N/", "page_name": "halsey palsey 🥢", "post_text": "722 likes, 9 comments - halseyskitchenn on March 24, 2026: &quot;✨ TAIWANESE BEEF NOODLE SOUP (Mì bò Đài Loan) ✨\\nServes 4–5\\nCooking time: ~2–2.5 hours\\n\\nRich, aromatic broth with tender beef 🍜🤍\\n\\n⸻\\nINGREDIENTS\\n\\nBeef &amp; Base\\n• 1 kg beef shank, cut into 2-inch chunks\\n• 2 tbsp oil\\n• 3–4 slices ginger\\n• 3 cloves garlic\\n• 2 scallions, cut into ~5 cm pieces\\n• 1 onion, cut into wedges\\n• 1 tomato, cut into chunks\\n• 1 tbsp tomato paste\\n• 1-2 tbsp chilli bean sauce (Toban Djan) OR chilli oil of choice\\n\\nBroth &amp; Seasoning \\n• 1 tsp sugar\\n• 60g soy sauce (mix light + dark soy sauce 1:1)\\n• 60g Shaoxing wine\\n• 3 bay leaves\\n• Mixed spice (2 star anise, 1 cinnamon stick, 3 cloves, 1 tsp coriander seeds, 1 black cardamom pod, 1/2 tsp fennel seeds) - IT’S OKAY TO MISS SOME\\n• 1/2 tsp five-spice powder\\n• 1/2 tsp pepper\\n\\nTo Serve\\n• Noodles of choice\\n• Bok choy\\n• Pickled mustard greens (optional)\\n• Extra chili oil\\n\\n⸻\\nINSTRUCTIONS\\n\\n1️⃣ Blanch the Beef\\nPlace the beef in a pot with water, 2 slices of ginger, and a splash of Shaoxing wine.\\nBring to a boil for 5 minutes to remove impurities.\\nDrain the beef, rinse it under running water. Set the cleaned beef aside.\\n\\n2️⃣ Toast the Aromatics &amp; Spices\\n(Optional) Toast the dry spices on a pan over low heat for 1-2 minutes until aromatic. Transfer them to a spice bag or tea filter to use later.\\n\\nIn the same pan, heat 2 tbsp oil over medium heat.\\nAdd ginger, garlic, scallions, onion, and tomato.\\nCook until fragrant and softened.\\nAdd chili paste (or chili oil) and tomato paste, then cook for 2–3 minutes to deepen the flavor.\\n\\n3️⃣ Build the Broth\\nReturn the beef to the pot.\\nAdd sugar, soy sauce, Shaoxing wine, and enough water to cover the beef.\\n\\nAdd the spice bag, bay leaves, five-spice powder, and black pepper.\\nBring to a boil, then reduce heat to low.\\n\\n4️⃣ Slow Simmer\\nCover and simmer for 1.5–2 hours, until the beef becomes very tender and the broth rich and aromatic. Taste &amp; adjust the seasoning to your liking.\\n\\n5️⃣ Prepare Noodles &amp; Vegetables\\nCook noodles according to package instructions.\\nBlanch bok choy in boiling water for 60s or until tender.\\nPlace noodles &amp; bok choy in a bowl.\\nLadle the hot broth &amp; meat over the noodles.\\nAdd pickled mustard greens and extra chili oil if desired.\\n\\n#noodles #asianfood&quot;.", "source_file": "data/instagram/raw/meili_mi_bo_dai_loan/instagram_all_posts.json", "fnb_relevance": {"branch_hits": [], "negative_hits": ["season"], "positive_hits": ["mì bò", "đài loan", "food"], "is_relevant_fnb": true, "relevance_score": 6, "generic_brand_hits": [], "explicit_brand_hits": ["mì bò đài loan"]}, "post_created_at": "2026-05-15T08:05:35.228873+00:00", "post_keyword_match": true, "parent_keyword_match": true, "post_keyword_matches": ["Mì Bò Đài Loan"]}	722 likes, 9 comments - halseyskitchenn on March 24, 2026: &quot;✨ TAIWANESE BEEF NOODLE SOUP (Mì bò Đài Loan) ✨\nServes 4–5\nCooking time: ~2–2.5 hours\n\nRich, aromatic broth with tender beef 🍜🤍\n\n⸻\nINGREDIENTS\n\nBeef &amp; Base\n• 1 kg beef shank, cut into 2-inch chunks\n• 2 tbsp oil\n• 3–4 slices ginger\n• 3 cloves garlic\n• 2 scallions, cut into ~5 cm pieces\n• 1 onion, cut into wedges\n• 1 tomato, cut into chunks\n• 1 tbsp tomato paste\n• 1-2 tbsp chilli bean sauce (Toban Djan) OR chilli oil of choice\n\nBroth &amp; Seasoning \n• 1 tsp sugar\n• 60g soy sauce (mix light + dark soy sauce 1:1)\n• 60g Shaoxing wine\n• 3 bay leaves\n• Mixed spice (2 star anise, 1 cinnamon stick, 3 cloves, 1 tsp coriander seeds, 1 black cardamom pod, 1/2 tsp fennel seeds) - IT’S OKAY TO MISS SOME\n• 1/2 tsp five-spice powder\n• 1/2 tsp pepper\n\nTo Serve\n• Noodles of choice\n• Bok choy\n• Pickled mustard greens (optional)\n• Extra chili oil\n\n⸻\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\n1️⃣ Blanch the Beef\nPlace the beef in a pot with water, 2 slices of ginger, and a splash of Shaoxing wine.\nBring to a boil for 5 minutes to remove impurities.\nDrain the beef, rinse it under running water. Set the cleaned beef aside.\n\n2️⃣ Toast the Aromatics &amp; Spices\n(Optional) Toast the dry spices on a pan over low heat for 1-2 minutes until aromatic. Transfer them to a spice bag or tea filter to use later.\n\nIn the same pan, heat 2 tbsp oil over medium heat.\nAdd ginger, garlic, scallions, onion, and tomato.\nCook until fragrant and softened.\nAdd chili paste (or chili oil) and tomato paste, then cook for 2–3 minutes to deepen the flavor.\n\n3️⃣ Build the Broth\nReturn the beef to the pot.\nAdd sugar, soy sauce, Shaoxing wine, and enough water to cover the beef.\n\nAdd the spice bag, bay leaves, five-spice powder, and black pepper.\nBring to a boil, then reduce heat to low.\n\n4️⃣ Slow Simmer\nCover and simmer for 1.5–2 hours, until the beef becomes very tender and the broth rich and aromatic. Taste &amp; adjust the seasoning to your liking.\n\n5️⃣ Prepare Noodles &amp; Vegetables\nCook noodles according to package instructions.\nBlanch bok choy in boiling water for 60s or until tender.\nPlace noodles &amp; bok choy in a bowl.\nLadle the hot broth &amp; meat over the noodles.\nAdd pickled mustard greens and extra chili oil if desired.\n\n#noodles #asianfood&quot;.	2026-05-15 16:49:43.046066+07
